-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Container images and VM disk images
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The published container images are built on Alpine Linux, pinned by digest in
the Dockerfiles that build them; the console (admin-ui) also carries the Node.js
runtime, copied from the official Node.js image, with Node.js's licence beside it
(NODEJS_LICENSE). The database runs the official PostgreSQL image, pinned by
digest in stowage.yaml. The VM disk images are built on the Kairos operating
system. Each image names its base in its org.opencontainers.image.base.name label
and carries this NOTICE and the LICENSE under /usr/share/licenses/streamscopeai/,
beside a THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES list of the libraries it bundles (the proxy,
admin-api and admin-ui images; `ssai licenses` prints the CLI's).
These bases contain software under the GNU GPL and other licences; their
corresponding sources are published by their projects (Alpine aports, Node.js,
the PostgreSQL official image, Kairos and its Ubuntu base).

This product includes data derived from third-party open-source projects.

